# =============================================================================
# Hermes Agent — Secrets (.env)
# =============================================================================
# Destination: ~/.hermes/.env  (NOT in this repo)
# This file holds API keys and tokens ONLY. Everything else (model selection,
# fallbacks, toolsets, memory settings) lives in config.yaml.
#
# Precedence (highest first):
#   1. CLI flags         e.g.  hermes chat --model claude-sonnet-4-6
#   2. ~/.hermes/config.yaml
#   3. ~/.hermes/.env    ← you are here
#   4. Built-in defaults
# =============================================================================


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — Anthropic API key (primary provider)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-REPLACE_ME


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RECOMMENDED — OpenRouter (one key, hundreds of models)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Even if you only use Claude, this is worth ~$5 of credits because:
#   • It's the fallback when Anthropic rate-limits you mid-session.
#   • It unlocks the `moa` (mixture-of-agents) tool.
#   • Lets you test GPT/Gemini/DeepSeek/Qwen with `hermes model` cheaply.
#
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys  (pay-as-you-go, no monthly fee)
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-REPLACE_ME


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RECOMMENDED — GitHub token (higher rate limits for code/skills search)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this you get 60 GitHub API requests/hour, which hits its limit fast
# when Hermes browses the Skills Hub or analyzes repos.
# Generate a CLASSIC token with NO scopes at:
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens/new   (no permissions needed)
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_REPLACE_ME


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — High-quality search (pick one based on your use case)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXA: best for research/investment/learning — semantic search, paper filters.
#   https://exa.ai
# EXA_API_KEY=

# Tavily: solid general-purpose with a free tier.
#   https://tavily.com
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Firecrawl: scrape full sites cleanly (good for investment data).
#   https://firecrawl.dev
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Local LLM (Ollama)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ollama runs on http://localhost:11434 and needs no API key. Wiring is in
# config.yaml under `providers.ollama`. Switch to it with:
#   /model custom:ollama:qwen2.5-coder:32b
#
# IMPORTANT: Hermes requires models with ≥64K context. Start Ollama with:
#   OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=65536 ollama serve


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Messaging gateways
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave commented until you run `hermes gateway setup`.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
